## 6. DIMENSION EFFECT — the primary finding
- Instruction **dimension** explains **19.3%** of sensitivity variance vs **1.7%** for the Pool A/B split — i.e. dimension explains ~11x more sensitivity variance than pool.
- **Mixed-effects test (headline, valid unit):** `sensitivity ~ dimension + (1|seed) + (1|article)` → LRT χ²=30.8, df=13, **p=0.003632** (significant). Variance: seed=0.0022, article=0.0063, residual=0.0159.
  - _seed-aggregated Kruskal-Wallis (cruder, underpowered — 50 seeds / 14 dims):_ H=23.5, p=0.03647
  - _robust to quality:_ dimension ranking is Spearman 0.94 between raw and quality-residualized Sensitivity (not a quality artifact).
  - _robust to thin dimensions:_ dropping single-seed dimensions (Meta-reflection) leaves η²=0.187 (vs 0.193 with all), mixed-model p=0.00392 — dimension effect is ROBUST to dropping single-seed dimensions.

